│▌  Start here              │                                                                                                                                  │
│   How it works            │ Welcome to Sendito. This help explains how the app works and shows the                                                           │
│ Tutorials                 │ steps for the most common tasks.                                                                                                 │
│   First request           │                                                                                                                                  │
│   Save and organize       │ Sendito sends requests and shows their responses: HTTP, gRPC, WebSocket,                                                         │
│   Environments            │ SSE, MQTT and MCP tools. Each request is a text file in a folder (the                                                            │
│   Secrets and auth        │ collection). You can edit the files in any editor and keep them in git.                                                          │
│   Chain requests          │                                                                                                                                  │
│   Read a response         │ ── Use this help ──                                                                                                              │
│   Import and export       │   •  Press Tab or Shift+Tab to open the next or the previous section, or click a name in the list on the left.                   │
│   gRPC call               │   •  Type a word to search the open section. Press Enter for the next match.                                                     │
│   Streams (WS, SSE, MQTT) │   •  Press Esc or F1 to close the help.                                                                                          │
│   MCP tools               │   •  The command :help <name> opens the section with that name, for example :help grpc.                                          │
│   Run a folder            │   •  The help shows your keys. When you change a key, the help shows the new key.                                                │
│   Customize               │                                                                                                                                  │
│ Keys                      │ The list on the left has four groups:                                                                                            │
│   All keys                │   Guide          How the screen and the requests work.                                                                           │
│   Global                  │   Tutorials      Steps for the most common tasks. Start with "First request".                                                    │
│   Sidebar tree            │   Keys           All the keys, the marks on the screen and the commands.                                                         │
│   Text editing            │   Functions      The functions that a request field or a script can call.                                                        │
│   Tables                  │                                                                                                                                  │
│   Response                │ ── The screen ──                                                                                                                 │
│   Query (jq)              │   Top bar        The open request tabs, the active environment and the help key.                                                 │
│   Dialogs                 │   Sidebar        The request tree of the collection, or the history.                                                             │
│   Fixed keys              │   URL card       The method (or the protocol), the address and the Send button.                                                  │
│   Symbols                 │   Request pane   The parts of the request, in tabs (Params, Headers, Body, Auth, Scripts, Options, Docs).                        │
│   Commands                │   Response pane  The response, in tabs (Body, Headers, Timing, Results).                                                         │
│ Functions                 │   Footer         The state on the left. On the right, the keys for the part that has the focus.                                  │
│   Template functions      │                                                                                                                                  │
│   Send-time values        │ ── Move around ──                                                                                                                │
│   Lua scripts             │   •  Press Tab to move the focus to the next field or pane. Press Shift+Tab to move it back.                                     │
│   Lua catalog             │   •  Press Ctrl+W, then a direction: Ctrl+W h, Ctrl+W j, Ctrl+W k or Ctrl+W l go to the pane in that direction.                  │
│                           │   •  Press Ctrl+W and stop: a menu shows all the keys that can come next.                                                        │
│                           │   •  Press Ctrl+W ] to open the next tab of the focused pane (for example, Params to Headers).                                   │
│                           │   •  Press Ctrl+W z to make the focused pane full size. Press it again to restore it.                                            │
│                           │   •  Click a pane, a tab, a row or a button to use it. The wheel scrolls the pane under the pointer.                             │
│                           │                                                                                                                                  │
│                           │ ── The keys to know first ──                                                                                                     │
│                           │   •  Ctrl+N: open a new HTTP request.                                                                                            │
│                           │   •  Ctrl+Enter: send the request.                                                                                               │
│                           │   •  Ctrl+W x: stop the request that runs.                                                                                       │
│                           │   •  Ctrl+S: save the request to a file.                                                                                         │
│                           │   •  Ctrl+P: open the command palette. Type a part of an action name, or ":" and a command.                                      │
│                           │   •  F4: choose the environment.                                                                                                 │
│                           │   •  Ctrl+W ,: open the settings.                                                                                                │
│                           │   •  Ctrl+W q: quit Sendito.                                                                                                     │
│                           │                                                                                                                                  │
│                           │ The footer always shows the keys for the part that has the focus. When you                                                       │
│                           │ do not know the next step, look at the footer or press Ctrl+W.                                                                   │
